{
  "id": "EDU044",
  "title": "The Same Request Wears Two Coats",
  "family": "learning",
  "category": "language/communication",
  "premise": "A teammate needs the same missing file from a close colleague and an unfamiliar organizer, but copies a context-heavy shorthand message to both. Adding necessary context adapts the second request without changing its purpose.",
  "hook": "What does this reader already know?",
  "visible_action": "A compact request bubble gains file name, deadline context, and greeting blocks as its audience marker changes.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Adapt context and tone to the reader while preserving the underlying request.",
  "gate": "Avoid treating one cultural register as universally correct or inventing the sender’s feelings.",
